  "thesis_summary": {
    "thesis": "Deutsche B\u00f6rse Group is a leading European market infrastructure operator spanning exchanges, clearing, custody, fund distribution, indices, and buy-side software. **[Fact]** Four segments cover the transaction value chain: Investment Management Solutions (SimCorp, ISS STOXX indices and ESG data), Trading & Clearing (Eurex derivatives, Xetra cash equities, commodities, FX and digital assets), Fund Services (Clearstream fund connectivity), and Securities Services (custody, settlement, fund processing). **[Fact]** FY2025 net revenue was **\u20ac6,026 million** (+3% versus **\u20ac5,829 million** in 2024); net revenue excluding treasury result was **\u20ac5,189 million** (+9%). EBITDA was **\u20ac3,512 million** and EBITDA excluding treasury result **\u20ac2,675 million** (+14%). Net profit attributable to shareholders was **\u20ac1,995 million**; diluted earnings per share **\u20ac10.90** and cash earnings per share **\u20ac11.65** (`investor-documents/ir-db1/annual_report_2025.pdf`, Results of operations). **[Fact]** Q1 2026 net revenue excluding treasury result was **\u20ac1,434 million** (+12% versus **\u20ac1,277 million**); EBITDA excluding treasury result **\u20ac683 million** (+18%); net profit attributable to Deutsche B\u00f6rse AG shareholders **\u20ac585 million** (+11%) (`investor-documents/ir-db1/quarterly_statement_q1_2026.pdf`). The company earns toll-like fees on trading, clearing, data, and fund workflows with minimal balance-sheet principal risk on core operations.",
    "why_market_wrong": "No dated structural discount or yield-curve setup. **[Inference]** Q1 2026 acceleration (+12% net revenue ex treasury, +18% EBITDA ex treasury) reflects elevated volatility in rates, commodities, and equities; the market may treat that pace as durable. **[Inference]** Declining treasury result (net interest from clearing cash) masks operating strength: total net revenue grew only 9% in Q1 2026 while operating segments grew faster. We normalize on FY2025 owner cash flow, not Q1 2026 peak volumes. **Predictive attribute:** none (franchise earnings at price, not market-structure exclusion).",
